# Unit 398: learn router, Rules and Closing checklist cut to the mode-wide rules (L4, QT-01, QT-02); only assess writes achieved (L1, QT-10)
every objective's state names the evidence that produced it => plan.md progress.md: "Every state names its evidence"
confidence was asked before each correction, and recorded => tutor.md Ask for confidence before you look; "Record the pair in the calibration table on every corrected delivery"
reviews are scheduled per objective, with dates => retain.md The ladder: "Dates are per OA-NN, never per topic"; Done when
the closing report says what they can do now and what they still cannot => assess.md The closing report
the solution of an exercise lives in a different file and is written after delivery => exercises.md The solution is another file, written after delivery; router Where it lands: "solutions/, each written only after its delivery"
measure before teaching => plan.md Probe before you write anything: "Do not ask what the person knows"
is the problem, not the input => plan.md Probe before you write anything (moved there in 398)
ask the person only what only they can answer => plan.md Ask only what only they can answer
an objective is something observable they will be able to do unaided => plan.md Objectives: "Observable, and unaided"
ask for their confidence before correcting => tutor.md Ask for confidence before you look
high confidence with a wrong result is the dangerous cell => tutor.md table: "The dangerous one: they are not going to check this again"
hints climb a ladder, one step per request => tutor.md One hint rung per request
if the person asks for the solution, give it => router Rules: "a solution they ask for is given"; tutor.md When they ask for the solution: "Give it"
and record the objective as not acquired, back into review => tutor.md When they ask for the solution: solved by the system, shortest review interval
retrieval, not rereading => teach.md Close with retrieval, not a summary; retain.md Running a review
assessment uses a new case => router Rules: "A different case each time"; assess.md: "A new case, always"
never edit the record to be kind => tutor.md What you write: "Never edit an earlier line to be kind"; plan.md: "A sixth word invented to be kind"
